From 4ff5108763c8dcda6809bfabed18af9417ec7274 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:38:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): alert a dead sync watcher through the hub
 courier [daveey]

Example incident: ContainmentRefused repeatedly killed kanban_sync_watcher across gateways
during repeated failures. Supervisor gave up restarts; dispatch stayed on
claim_deferred(sync_first_round). replica-stale logged at 20 min through the local outbox,
which could not push because sync was the thing that died.

The receipt identity fix (_certified ignores Board row seq/version/updated_at/hlc) landed
separately in #3753 (4124f7c4ae). This change is the detector only.

Why not caught: replica-stale files through the dead outbox; SchemaAhead already uses the
hermes-hub courier, a watcher crash did not.

Fix: on each dispatcher tick, a `.sync-state.json` crash record older than 5 min opens one
hub card via the courier (comment while open). Graceful STOPPED and SchemaAhead are other
alarms. The 60 s outbox throttle does not skip this check.

Proof: test_kanban_sync_watcher_alert: crash <5 min silent; at 5 min hub create-task; same
incident no duplicate; new incident comments; STOPPED/SchemaAhead skip; dispatcher tick
still calls it when the outbox throttle would skip.

Card: t_eeeeee000000001f

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
